<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">chronicle</ansi>

Your company keeps a chronicle: a running record of the deeds it is known
for, written down as they happen and read back in plain sentences, newest
first. It is the company's own story of what it did.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Reading it</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">chronicle</ansi>           the newest 12 deeds, and a count of every deed ever
  <ansi fg="command">chronicle 2</ansi>         the next page
  <ansi fg="command">chronicle boss</ansi>      only one kind (see the list below; <ansi fg="command">chronicle lore</ansi> for beast lore); add a page number to turn it
  <ansi fg="command">chronicle all</ansi>       every deed kept, with <ansi fg="command">chronicle all relics</ansi> for one kind

In the web client the Company window has a Chronicle tab: the same deeds,
with a button to filter by kind. It fits a phone as it does the desktop.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What is written down</ansi>

  joined       someone signed on (<ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>)
  dismissed    someone was sent away
  deserted     someone lost faith and left (<ansi fg="command">help alignment</ansi>)
  fallen       a member died: you, or a companion (<ansi fg="command">help death</ansi>)
  raised       a fallen companion was raised
  lost         a fallen companion was not raised in time
  defeats      the company was beaten, and what became of it (<ansi fg="command">help defeat</ansi>)
  bosses       a boss, the master of a lair, was killed
  relics       a relic was found (<ansi fg="command">help relics</ansi>)
  mercy        a beaten foe was spared (<ansi fg="command">help mercy</ansi>)
  executions   a beaten foe was put to death (<ansi fg="command">help mercy</ansi>)
  promotions   someone took a new class (<ansi fg="command">help classes</ansi>)
  stories      a scene on the road ended, and how (<ansi fg="command">help events</ansi>)
  awakenings   a relic woke a new power while it was worn (<ansi fg="command">help awakenings</ansi>)
  errands      a companion came home from an errand (<ansi fg="command">help errands</ansi>)
  groups       a band you held a bounty on was broken, every foe down (<ansi fg="command">help bounties</ansi>)
  bounties     a bounty was claimed at a board (<ansi fg="command">help bounties</ansi>)
  rites        the company held rites for a companion gone for good, or let it pass (<ansi fg="command">help rites</ansi>)
  lore         the company learned a creature's habits (the 6th kill of a kind, the 3rd of a boss) (<ansi fg="command">help bestiary</ansi>)

Each deed names who was involved, where it happened and how long ago.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What to know</ansi>

  - It belongs to the company, which is its leader: it is kept through a
    restart and a copyover, and goes only when the character is deleted.
  - It keeps the newest 300 deeds. The count at the bottom of
    <ansi fg="command">chronicle</ansi> never forgets: it includes the deeds that have scrolled off.
  - Beast lore is written once per kind, and only for kinds learned from now
    on. The chronicle keeps the newest 30 of those lines, apart from the 300.
  - Times are real time. Nothing here moves the world's clock, and reading
    it costs nothing, even in a fight.
  - The chronicle only remembers. It gives no gold, experience or power.

Townsfolk speak of these deeds, once each (<ansi fg="command">help townsfolk</ansi>).

See also: <ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help events</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help webclient</ansi>.
